  Here's an analogy. In the roman days a top advisor would be given a ring that acted like a stamp a wax seal/signature. It was used to sign letters so you knew it was from the emporors advisor. 
  A private key is like a wax seal stamped with a signet ring that only you own. 
  Anyone can look at the seal and recognise it as yours. Only your ring could have made it, though, so you can't later say "I didn't send that letter."
This signet ring is like a private key and only you have this signet ring. 
  
